+Tailored Operator Runbook — Convert Aegis scaffold → validated production (CUSTOM)
+
+Purpose
+- Step-by-step, copy-and-run playbook tuned to your representative hardware. Replace placeholders marked with <...>.
+
+Prerequisites
+- Representative hardware:
+  - ECU/controller hostnames (SSH accessible from operator runner): <ECU_HOSTS>, e.g. "ecu-1.example.com"
+  - CAN interfaces (can0/can1) and TSN NIC names (eth1) on those hosts
+  - HIL rig accessible from operator runner
+  - Self-hosted runners and builders (labels: aegis/role=builder, aegis/role=hardware, aegis/npu=<vendor>)
+- Secrets configured in environment or CI:
+  - COSIGN_KMS_URI (KMS URI for cosign key)
+  - REKOR_SERVER
+  - WATTTIME_API_KEY
+  - S3_UPLOAD (evidence bucket)
+  - CERTIFIER_API_TOKEN (optional)
+  - NPU_RUNNERS (comma-separated)
+
+Files created by this runbook (out dir)
+- <OUT>/rt_proofs/*/rt_slo_proof.json
+- <OUT>/hil_cert/* (campaign outputs, waveform compares)
+- <OUT>/perception/* (sim outputs, failures.json, adv_data.ndjson)
+- <OUT>/evidence_manifest.json
+- <OUT>/auditor_bundle.tar.gz (signed when COSIGN set)
+
+High-level sequence (single representative run)
+1) Preflight — verify runners & tools
+   - On each builder/runner: sudo /bin/bash ops/infra/hardening/check_runner_hardening.sh
+   - Ensure vendor SDKs present: ops/infra/hardening/install_vendor_sdks.sh VENDOR=<vendor>
+
+2) RT sweep & signed proofs
+   - Create a targets list: ops/av/rt/rt_sweep_targets.json
+     Example:
+       [{"host":"<ECU_HOST_1>","iface":"can0"}, {"host":"<ECU_HOST_2>","iface":"can0"}]
+   - Run:
+       OUT=<OUT> TARGETS="<ECU_HOST_1>:can0,<ECU_HOST_2>:can0" COSIGN_KMS_URI=$COSIGN_KMS_URI S3_UPLOAD=$S3_UPLOAD \
+         ./ops/validation/run_rt_sweep_and_sign.sh "$OUT/rt_proofs"
+   - Acceptance (example):
+       * p99 loop jitter <= 0.5 ms (adjust per vehicle)
+       * safe_stop_ms <= vehicle-specific threshold (compute with ops/av/slo/vehicle_slo_table.py)
+   - If fail: python3 ops/validation/rt_remediation_agent.py --report <proof> --out <proof>/remediation.json
+
+3) Exhaustive HIL campaigns + formal closure
+   - Prepare scenario runners list: ops/av/certification/<vehicle>_scenarios.txt (one command per line)
+   - Run iterative certification loop:
+       COSIGN_KMS_URI=$COSIGN_KMS_URI ./ops/robotics/control/certified/run_exhaustive_hil_and_close_formal.sh \
+         --scenarios-file ops/av/certification/<vehicle>_scenarios.txt --golden /opt/aegis/golden_trace.ndjson --out "$OUT/hil_cert" --cosign "$COSIGN_KMS_URI" --max-iter 5
+   - Acceptance:
+       * All critical scenarios ran_ok=true and compare_ok=true in campaign_summary.json
+       * Apalache reports no unresolved counterexamples for safety invariants
+   - Produce signed HIL cert bundle (cosign) and upload to S3
+
+4) Perception large-scale sim → HIL → retrain → NPU validation
+   - Run full pipeline:
+       ./ops/av/perception/scale/run_sim_hil_field_pipeline.sh --packs 20 --per-pack 200 --parallel 6 --out "$OUT/perception" --npu-runners "$NPU_RUNNERS" --cosign "$COSIGN_KMS_URI"
+   - Collect adversarial dataset and retrain:
+       adv dataset: $OUT/perception/adv_dataset/adv_data.ndjson
+       auto retrain invoked by pipeline (check $OUT/perception/retrain)
+   - Validate ONNX artifacts on each NPU runner (auto_retrain_pipeline attempts this)
+   - Acceptance:
+       * Perception FN rate in certified envelope <= 1e-3 (domain dependent)
+       * All ONNX artifacts smoke-tested on NPU runners and signed
+
+5) Ensure builder hardening & provenance
+   - On each builder host:
+       sudo ./ops/infra/hardening/provision_and_label_runners.sh LABELS="role=builder,npu=true"
+       sudo /bin/bash ops/infra/hardening/check_runner_hardening.sh
+   - Run provenance enforcer locally or in CI:
+       IMAGE_MANIFESTS=deploy.yaml REKOR_SERVER=$REKOR_SERVER python3 ops/ci/promotion_gate/enforce_builder_provenance.py
+   - Acceptance: enforcement exits 0 only if images cosign-signed and Rekor entries present
+
+6) Carbon monitor & enforce with override workflow
+   - Monitor mode (14 days recommended):
+       python3 ops/carbon/monitor_tune.py --duration-s 1209600 --interval-s 300 --region <REGION> --out "$OUT/carbon_tune.json"
+   - Tune threshold and add to CI secrets AEGIS_CARBON_THRESHOLD
+   - For emergency promotions, Platform Owner signs override:
+       python3 ops/carbon/override_signer.py --approval-id <ID> --approved-by owner@example.com --scope '{"manifests":"deploy.yaml"}' --out /tmp/override.json
+       cosign verify /tmp/override.json
+
+7) Build auditor evidence bundle & submit
+   - Build/manifest:
+       python3 ops/certifier/auditor_package_builder.py --artifacts-root . --out "$OUT/auditor_bundle.tar.gz" --manifest-out "$OUT/evidence_manifest.json" --cosign-key "$COSIGN_KMS_URI" --s3 "$S3_UPLOAD" --vehicle <VEHICLE>
+   - Submit & track findings:
+       python3 ops/certifier/submit_and_track_findings.py --bundle "$OUT/auditor_bundle.tar.gz" --upload-url "<CERT_UPLOAD_URL>" --findings-url "<CERT_FINDINGS_URL>" --api-token "$CERTIFIER_API_TOKEN" --outdir "$OUT/certifier_findings"
+   - Acceptance: certifier issues "accepted" or a finite list of findings with remediation timeline; critical findings closed
+
+Incident triage & escalation
+- If a critical failure occurs (safe-stop miss, HIL critical failure), execute ops/runbooks/incident_triage_playbook.md and notify Controls Lead / Safety Officer immediately with bundle path.
+
+Recordkeeping & audit
+- All runs should call ops.sdk.evidence_sdk.record_manifest (scripts already include this).
+- Keep evidence in S3 with proper retention and access controls per ops/governance/evidence_retention_policy.md
+
+Notes
+- Replace all placeholders (<...>) with your environment values before running.
+- Maintain scenario files, golden traces and acceptance thresholds under version control.
+
